AUDIT-009,current assets were what percent of net assets acquired for the can and alcan transactions?,"To calculate the percent of net assets acquired that were current assets for the U.S. Can and Alcan transactions, I need to:

1. Identify the current assets acquired in each transaction
2. Calculate the total net assets acquired for each transaction
3. Divide the current assets by the total net assets and multiply by 100 to get the percentage

For the U.S. Can transaction:
Current assets acquired = ""other assets primarily inventories and receivables"" = $218.8 million
Total net assets acquired = $617.9 million
Percent of net assets that were current assets = $218.8 million / $617.9 million x 100 = 35.4%

For the Alcan transaction:
Current assets acquired = ""other assets primarily inventories and receivables"" = $40.7 million 
Total net assets acquired = $184.7 million
Percent of net assets that were current assets = $40.7 million / $184.7 million x 100 = 22.0%

So the current assets were 35.4% of the net assets acquired for the U.S. Can transaction, and 22.0% of the net assets acquired for the Alcan transaction.","[1] page 51 of 98 notes to consolidated financial statements ball corporation and subsidiaries 3 . acquisitions ( continued ) effective january 1 , 2007 . the acquisition has been accounted for as a purchase and , accordingly , its results have been included in the consolidated financial statements since march 27 , 2006 . alcan packaging on march 28 , 2006 , ball acquired north american plastic bottle container assets from alcan packaging ( alcan ) for $ 184.7 million cash . the acquired assets included two plastic container manufacturing plants in the u.s . and one in canada , as well as certain manufacturing equipment and other assets from other alcan facilities . this acquisition strengthens the company 2019s plastic container business and complements its food container business . the acquired business primarily manufactures and sells barrier polypropylene plastic bottles used in food packaging and , to a lesser extent , barrier pet plastic bottles used for beverages and food . the acquired operations formed part of ball 2019s plastic packaging , americas , segment during 2006 . the acquisition has been accounted for as a purchase and , accordingly , its results have been included i...

