AUDIT-090,Summarize the following news within 93 words:,"Texas Attorney General Ken Paxton has filed a lawsuit against the Biden administration, seeking to prevent federal agents from cutting razor wire at the border. Paxton argues that the White House is undermining Texas' efforts to ensure border security amidst a surge in immigration. Environmental and immigration advocates have raised concerns about the razor wire, citing its impact on the environment and human safety. Texas and the federal government have been at odds over border issues, with the Department of Justice previously suing Texas over the installation of buoys and Governor Greg Abbott planning to restart construction on border walls.","[1] Texas once again heads to court — this time trying to stop feds from cutting razor wire at border
Texas Attorney General Ken Paxton is back in action, filing suit against the Biden administration Tuesday, hoping to stop federal agents from cutting razor wire at the border.
In the suit, Paxton alleges that the White House is ""undermining"" efforts by the state to ensure security amid record numbers of immigrants coming to the Texas border.
“Texas has the sovereign right to construct border barriers to prevent the entry of illegal aliens,” Paxton said in a press release.
Environmental and immigration advocates have raised concerns about the razor wire at the border and its implications for the environment and human safety, according to the Associated Press.
The ""concertina wire"" barriers have reportedly injured migrants as they have tried to cross into Texas along the Rio Grande in border cities such as Brownsville and Eagle Pass. In some cases, federal agents have had to cut the wire to free to the migrants caught in it, according to the AP.
The state has repeatedly butted heads and gone to court with the federal government as efforts ramp up to curtail illegal crossings at the Texas...",,,,
